94"} "2020"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/42"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "400 metres, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "4 –  7 August 2024"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2157"} "Stade de France, Saint-Denis, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2013536"} "45 from 31 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "There was no clear favorite in this event, although British runner " [:a {:href "/athletes/133975"} "Matt Hudson-Smith"] " was probably a slight favorite. " [:a {:href "/athletes/120724"} "Kirani James"] " (GRN), the 2012 gold medalist, was still a contender, as were the 2020 champion, " [:a {:href "/athletes/132635"} "Steven Gardiner"] " (BAH), and the 2016 gold medalist, " [:a {:href "/athletes/135688"} "Wayde van Niekerk"] ". Van Niekerk opted to run only the 200 in Paris, however, and Gardiner withdrew a few days before the event."] "\n\n" [:p {} "James, American " [:a {:href "/athletes/147342"} "Michael Norman"] ", and Hudson-Smith made the final, with James winning the second semi and Hudson-Smith the third, followed by Norman in second. The first semi was won by American " [:a {:href "/athletes/150676"} "Quincy Hall"] ", a former 400 hurdler who had won the USA Olympic Trials. James and Norman got out fast but Trinidad &amp; Tobago’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/146879"} "Jereem Richards"] " led as they entered the backstretch. Richards led at 200 metres in 20.46 but Hudson-Smith took over on the far turn, with Hall nowhere in sight. At the head of the stretch, Hudson-Smith led over Richards and James, with Hall fourth, but seemingly too far back, and Norman out of the medal chase."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Hall refused to concede and pulled ahead of James and Richards, and then outleaned Hudson-Smith in the last few strides, winning gold in 43.40, making him the #4 performer ever, as Hudson-Smith took silver in 43.44, breaking his own European record. Also finishing strongly was Zambia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/150698"} "Muzala Samukonga"] ", who took bronze just ahead of Richards, with James placing fifth, as Norman faded to last place. It was the deepest-ever 400 metre race, with best-ever marks-for-place set for 2-3-4-5."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Rep"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1309"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/150676"} "Quincy Hall"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "44.28 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "43.95 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "43.40 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "705"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/133975"} "Matt Hudson-Smith"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "44.78 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "44.07 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "43.44 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1378"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/150698"} "Muzala Samukonga"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ZAM"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ZAM.png"}] "ZAM"]] [:td {} "44.56 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "43.81 (2 h2)"] [:td {} "43.74 (3)"] [:td {} [:sp